    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the $4.00 no-show fee does not stand and is refunded to the rider in full. Both of you were at the Toa Payoh pickup, so this is not a wrong-entrance or pin problem and no one is accused of never turning up. The rider's device (EV-GPS-00402) recorded 47 clean fixes between 07:41:40 and 07:48:34, all stationary and all within 23 m of the pin; the driver's device recorded 22 clean fixes inside the 50 m pickup radius between 07:45:10 and 07:48:40. POL-NS-03 therefore has no purchase (and with registered_pickup_points at 1, its goodwill limb cannot be reached), and POL-NS-04 does not apply because the only party message in the chat log (EV-CHAT-00402) is the driver's 'here' at 07:41:50 - the rider sent nothing, so there is no unanswered rider message exonerating anyone. The case turns on the waiting period alone. For this trip the free waiting period in force was 300 seconds, read from EV-TRIP-00402 (platform_policy.free_wait_sec = 300; because the record carries its own figure, the 180-second default in fee_schedule.defaults does not apply). POL-NS-01(c) measures that wait from the first qualifying in-geofence GPS fix, not from the 'arrived' tap, and on EV-GPS-00402 the first in-geofence fix is at 07:45:10, running unbroken to the 07:48:40 cancellation - 210 seconds, 90 seconds short of the 300 required. The driver's own account of waiting 'the full five minutes and more' runs from his 07:41:40 tap, which is the measurement the clause expressly does not use; the rider is also right that no in-radius fix falls at or before that tap, so limb (b) is not satisfied on the trace either, and the outcome is unchanged. Under POL-NS-06 a waiting period not served means the fee is not chargeable and is refunded in full, whether or not the rider was present and whether or not the rider responded to messages. No driver compensation is payable: POL-NS-06 says so on a shortfall, and POL-NS-07 pays only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full. The driver's correct points stand - limb (a) is recorded, he did reach the pickup (22 consecutive in-radius fixes), the RIDER_NO_SHOW code is one limb (d) recognises, and the anti-farming check is not tripped (no_show_terminations_30d 1 against completed_trips_30d 120, and POL-GEN-01 allows no other field, including the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter, to be substituted) - but none of them cures the 90-second shortfall, which he does not dispute. The advisory EV-ADVIS-00402-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT), so POL-NS-06(i) cannot be used to sum intervals, and there is only one in-geofence interval in any case. The amount: EV-FARE-00402 carries a single cancellation-fee line of $4.00, payment_status CHARGED, agreeing with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of $4.00, with every other line at 0.00. No escalation and no referral: the deciding evidence is unimpaired under POL-NS-08 (no trace gap, no clock skew, a complete chat log, and a fare line that reconciles), confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no POL-NS-09 trigger fires, and no clause produces a referral. The $4.00 monetary effect is below the $8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05), so it executes on issue; this is a provisional ruling and either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
